{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38345450",
      "title": "Derived / Computed State",
      "sourceHash": "1434b15b51287e517a62bc2b54b2df59bc74c94f9feb8e3282c4095741eb67a2",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 4.29,
          "en": "So at this point in the section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.29,
          "end": 8.64,
          "en": "you already learned quite a bit about state, and events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.64,
          "end": 11.67,
          "en": "and a lot about React in general.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.67,
          "end": 15.6,
          "en": "Now, before we come to an end and conclude this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.6,
          "end": 16.8,
          "en": "I wanna dive into",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.8,
          "end": 21.03,
          "en": "another state related very important concept,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.03,
          "end": 26.03,
          "en": "and that's the concept of derived or computed state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.04,
          "end": 30.87,
          "en": "or derived or computed values as you could also say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.87,
          "end": 33.51,
          "en": "And to explore this concept,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.51,
          "end": 36.75,
          "en": "let's say that below the \"expenses filter\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.75,
          "end": 41.01,
          "en": "but above the \"expense item\" elements here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.01,
          "end": 43.77,
          "en": "I wanna show a little text in a paragraph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.77,
          "end": 45.727,
          "en": "And let's say that here, I wanna say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.727,
          "end": 50.727,
          "en": "\"Data for years 2019, 2021, and 2022 is hidden,\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 54,
          "end": 57.51,
          "en": "if the filter is set to 2020.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 57.51,
          "end": 60.6,
          "en": "If it's set to 2021,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 60.6,
          "end": 65.58,
          "en": "I of course wanna say \"2019, 2020, and 2022.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 65.58,
          "end": 68.28,
          "en": "So, I basically wanna list all the years",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 68.28,
          "end": 71.19,
          "en": "which are currently not selected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 71.19,
          "end": 74.67,
          "en": "Now this is actually a feature which I'll soon remove",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 74.67,
          "end": 77.78999999999999,
          "en": "because we don't actually need it here in this app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 77.78999999999999,
          "end": 80.58,
          "en": "but it is a feature that allows me to explore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 80.58,
          "end": 83.793,
          "en": "this important concept of derived values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 84.87,
          "end": 88.02,
          "en": "Because one way of implementing this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 88.02,
          "end": 91.59700000000001,
          "en": "would be to register a new state, which we could name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 91.59700000000001,
          "end": 93.99000000000001,
          "en": "\"filter info text,\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 93.99000000000001,
          "end": 98.88,
          "en": "with a \"set filter info text\" state updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 98.88,
          "end": 103.88,
          "en": "And the initial value here could be this string here maybe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 105.09,
          "end": 109.71000000000001,
          "en": "where we say, \"2019, 2021, 2022,\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 109.71000000000001,
          "end": 112.267,
          "en": "and then we dynamically output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 112.267,
          "end": 114.90299999999999,
          "en": "\"filter info text\" down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 116.82,
          "end": 120.87,
          "en": "And now, we could update this whenever the filter changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 120.87,
          "end": 125.87,
          "en": "Then we could check \"if selected year is equal to 2019,\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 127.44,
          "end": 131.67,
          "en": "and if that's the case, we call \"set filter info text,\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 131.67,
          "end": 136.67000000000002,
          "en": "and set this to \"2020, '21 and '22.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 140.617,
          "end": 145.44,
          "en": "\"Else if selected year is 2020,\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 145.44,
          "end": 150.44,
          "en": "we \"set filter info text\" to \"2019, '21 and '22,\" and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 154.77,
          "end": 159.06,
          "en": "We also would of course add the condition for '21,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 159.06,
          "end": 162.42000000000002,
          "en": "where we set the filter info text like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 162.42000000000002,
          "end": 167.163,
          "en": "And \"else\" for the last case, we would exclude '22.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 169.35,
          "end": 172.05,
          "en": "That's how we could implement this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 172.05,
          "end": 175.5,
          "en": "If we save this, we have this text here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 175.5,
          "end": 178.02,
          "en": "It's a bit hard to read because it's not styled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 178.02,
          "end": 180.9,
          "en": "because I'll delete it soon anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 180.9,
          "end": 184.32,
          "en": "But you can see that currently 2020 is excluded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 184.32,
          "end": 186.45,
          "en": "because that's the year I selected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 186.45,
          "end": 189.78,
          "en": "If I switch this to 2021 on the other hand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 189.78,
          "end": 194.28,
          "en": "this updates and '21 is now excluded in this list here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 194.28,
          "end": 197.34,
          "en": "and instead all the other years are mentioned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 197.34,
          "end": 200.46,
          "en": "Also, please keep in mind that the filter doesn't work yet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 200.46,
          "end": 203.07,
          "en": "which is why we see all these years.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 203.07,
          "end": 205.653,
          "en": "But, this text updates as expected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 206.94,
          "end": 207.81,
          "en": "Nonetheless,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 207.81,
          "end": 212.1,
          "en": "this is typically not how you should implement this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 212.1,
          "end": 213.66,
          "en": "Whilst it works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 213.66,
          "end": 217.2,
          "en": "you are managing an additional piece of state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 217.2,
          "end": 219.72,
          "en": "which in the end is redundant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 219.72,
          "end": 224.4,
          "en": "Because this state here is in the end based on this state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 224.4,
          "end": 226.07999999999998,
          "en": "The year we exclude",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 226.07999999999998,
          "end": 229.41,
          "en": "is the year we're managing in this state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 229.41,
          "end": 232.44,
          "en": "So we're managing two pieces of state here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 232.44,
          "end": 237.44,
          "en": "even though they both depend on the same source so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 237.63,
          "end": 240.09,
          "en": "One state would be enough here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 240.09,
          "end": 243.36,
          "en": "Instead of being managed as a standalone state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 243.36,
          "end": 246.99,
          "en": "which updates whenever the other state updates,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 246.99,
          "end": 251.73,
          "en": "we should manage the info text as a computed value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 251.73,
          "end": 256.73,
          "en": "And that's what that derived state or computed state concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 257.22,
          "end": 258.33,
          "en": "is all about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 258.33,
          "end": 260.76,
          "en": "If you are setting a state that in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 260.76,
          "end": 264.09,
          "en": "is directly related to another state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 264.09,
          "end": 267.48,
          "en": "you typically don't wanna manage this as a separate state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 267.48,
          "end": 270.36,
          "en": "Instead you just want to add a new variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 270.36,
          "end": 273.57,
          "en": "a good old variable in your component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 273.57,
          "end": 276.06,
          "en": "And that could now be the \"filter info text\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 276.06,
          "end": 279.06,
          "en": "which initially is this text here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 279.06,
          "end": 281.973,
          "en": "with the year 2020 excluded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 283.74,
          "end": 286.92,
          "en": "And then we can extract this \"if\" check here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 286.92,
          "end": 289.14,
          "en": "out of this handler function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 289.14,
          "end": 292.503,
          "en": "and also put it directly in this component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 293.49,
          "end": 296.85,
          "en": "So that there, we now check our filtered year.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 296.85,
          "end": 300.93,
          "en": "So this state on which this value in the end depends,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 300.93,
          "end": 304.65,
          "en": "we use this state in our \"if\" condition here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 304.65,
          "end": 306.9,
          "en": "and we simply set our variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 306.9,
          "end": 309.183,
          "en": "to those different pieces of text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 310.02,
          "end": 312.48,
          "en": "So instead of updating a separate state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 312.48,
          "end": 317.48,
          "en": "we just dynamically compute the value of this variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 317.64,
          "end": 320.19,
          "en": "and the value will be different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 320.19,
          "end": 323.403,
          "en": "depending on which state was selected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 324.39,
          "end": 326.88,
          "en": "This condition now also is redundant here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 326.88,
          "end": 331.35,
          "en": "since the value for this check here is our default anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 331.35,
          "end": 333.84000000000003,
          "en": "So, we can even get rid of that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 333.84000000000003,
          "end": 338.07,
          "en": "And now we have this leaner computed code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 338.07,
          "end": 341.67,
          "en": "which works because when the state is updated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 341.67,
          "end": 343.62,
          "en": "when this function here is called,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 343.62,
          "end": 348.36,
          "en": "this component function will re-execute again anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 348.36,
          "end": 351.63,
          "en": "So all this code here will be executed again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 351.63,
          "end": 353.85,
          "en": "and will derive a new value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 353.85,
          "end": 355.803,
          "en": "for \"filter info text\" therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 356.67,
          "end": 359.01,
          "en": "Hence, now I save everything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 359.01,
          "end": 362.43,
          "en": "we get exactly the same behavior as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 362.43,
          "end": 367.263,
          "en": "If I switch my state here, my filter, this value updates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 368.25,
          "end": 371.88,
          "en": "Even though the value itself is not managed as state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 371.88,
          "end": 374.13,
          "en": "but it's part of the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 374.13,
          "end": 377.13,
          "en": "that's re-executed when the state changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 377.13,
          "end": 380.463,
          "en": "and it then depends on the state that changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 381.57,
          "end": 384.12,
          "en": "So this here is a computed value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 384.12,
          "end": 387.66,
          "en": "a value which we derive based on this state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 387.66,
          "end": 390.9,
          "en": "And whilst you could also manage multiple states,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 390.9,
          "end": 393.33,
          "en": "and it wouldn't be a huge problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 393.33,
          "end": 395.763,
          "en": "using derived values like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 395.763,
          "end": 400.32,
          "en": "it's typically the more elegant and recommended approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 400.32,
          "end": 402.39,
          "en": "Here, I'll get rid of that though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 402.39,
          "end": 405.45,
          "en": "because we don't need that info text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 405.45,
          "end": 408.93,
          "en": "But knowing about this concept of derived state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 408.93,
          "end": 412.803,
          "en": "or derived values as it's also called, is important.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}